<http://data.silknow.org/object/0199153e-42ad-3db5-a3bb-708e6121702e/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "White linen corded bed cover with cotton back. The corded or quilted pattern was probably made with linen thread. The pattern includes a scattered floral arrangement with various flowers, leaves and stalks filling the field, and a cornucopia at each corner. The white cotton fringe attached on one end is probably original. Minor stains; ground slightly worn in spots."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0199153e-42ad-3db5-a3bb-708e6121702e> .

